# irregex — hardware-counter access for one helper, and nothing else.
#
# TEMPLATE. install.sh renders @USER@ and @DIGEST@ and validates the result with
# `visudo -c -f` before anything touches /etc/sudoers.d/. Do not install this
# file as-is; the placeholders are not valid sudoers syntax, which is deliberate
# — a stray `cp` of this file cannot become a live rule.
#
# WHAT THIS GRANTS
#   @USER@ may run exactly one absolute path as root, without a password, and
#   only if that file's SHA-256 still matches @DIGEST@.
#
#   The helper at that path forks, drops privileges irrevocably, and execs its
#   argument as @USER@. It never runs anything as root. So this rule does not
#   grant root — it grants ktrace/kperf ownership to one process at a time.
#
# WHY THE DIGEST IS THE LOAD-BEARING PART
#   Ten agent processes build in this repository concurrently. A NOPASSWD rule
#   naming a path any of them can write is a local root escalation, which is why
#   no rule here names anything under zig-out/ or any other build output. The
#   helper lives in a root-owned directory, mode 0555, and sudo re-hashes it on
#   every invocation: replace the binary and sudo refuses to run it. Changing the
#   helper therefore requires re-running install.sh under authentication — that
#   friction is the feature, not an oversight.
#
# WHAT IT STILL CANNOT PROTECT AGAINST
#   Anyone who can invoke the helper can nominate a process of their choosing to
#   receive counter access. That is a high-resolution timing side channel and a
#   kperf sampling facility, for one process, until it exits. It is much smaller
#   than root and it is not nothing. Read privilege/README.md before installing.
#
# REVOKE
#   sudo rm /etc/sudoers.d/irregex-pmu /usr/local/libexec/irregex-pmu-bless
#   Nothing else in the repository depends on it; every benchmark keeps working,
#   measuring cycles and instructions through the unprivileged backend.

# One line. NOPASSWD covers the authentication; a second `Defaults !authenticate`
# spec would be a redundant mechanism to audit, so there isn't one.
@USER@ ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: sha256:@DIGEST@ @HELPER@
